By 2015, Edward had been living in the Oceanicy Street Commission complex for 10 years. It was clear that all three men were of dubious character, but they assured police that Brendan had left Matthew Brennan's apartment weeks earlier to escape the ramifications of a botched drug deal. Unable to find proof of any such situation having occurred, police were convinced the men were lying. Then, one of Edward Hill's neighbors came forward. Eric, not his real name, provided a statement to police in which he claimed, Nippy told me it was him who killed Brendan Bernard. He said Brendan had been given $300 to score drugs, but he returned empty-handed with only $40 left. This prompted Edward to, quote, crack the shits. According to Eric, Edward bragged about killing Brendan, saying, It was easy. I hit him four times, and he just dropped.
到2015年，爱德华已经在海洋街公房大楼住了10年。很明显，这三个男人品行可疑，但他们向警方保证，布伦登几周前就离开了马修·布伦南的公寓，以逃避一次搞砸的毒品交易所带来的后果。在找不到任何此类情况发生的证据后，警方确信这些人在撒谎。然后，爱德华·希尔的一位邻居挺身而出。埃里克（化名）向警方提供了一份声明，他声称：“尼皮告诉我，是杀死布伦登·伯纳德的人。他说布伦登拿到了300澳元去买毒品，但他两手空空地回来了，只剩下40澳元。”这促使爱德华“发飙”。据埃里克说，爱德华吹嘘自己杀死了布伦登，并说：“这很简单。我打了四下，他就倒下了。”

25
00:32:03.000 --> 00:33:35.000
He said Brendan's body had been left in the bathtub for a week before being dismembered by Matthew Brennan and Konstantinos Balearis. Eric's statement was equal parts damning and chilling. However, police were aware that Edward Hill's claims were unreliable due to his intellectual disability, illicit drug use, and excessive alcohol consumption. Nevertheless, Eric stood by his statement, not only willing to testify in court, but also agreeing to serve as a police informant by wearing a concealed wire during further conversations with his neighbor. During these recorded conversations, Edward rambled on about Brendan Bernard, accusing him of trying to sell crushed glass disguised as crystal methamphetamine. Investigators were unable to prove whether these accusations were true, and Edward's unfounded stories only served to raise doubts as to the authenticity of his character, and thus, the validity of his claims that he was responsible for Brendan's death. Police were certain the truth of what happened to Brendan Bernard remained with those who were in Matthew Brennan's apartment on the afternoon of January 27. They brought Matthew, Konstantinos Balearis, and Edward Hill in for questioning, but all three men remained tight lipped regarding what exactly had happened.
他说布伦登的尸体在浴缸里放了一个星期，然后被马修·布伦南和康斯坦蒂诺斯·贝利亚里斯肢解。埃里克的声明既令人震惊又让人不寒而栗。然而，警方意识到爱德华·希尔的说法不可靠，因为他有智力残疾、吸毒和过度饮酒的问题。尽管如此，埃里克坚持他的陈述，不仅愿意在法庭上作证，还同意在与邻居的进一步对话中佩戴隐藏的窃听器担任警察线人。在这些录音对话中，爱德华喋喋不休地谈论着布伦登·伯纳德，指责他试图出售伪装成冰毒的碎玻璃。调查人员无法证明这些指控是否属实，爱德华毫无根据的故事只会引起人们对他品格真实性的怀疑，从而也怀疑他声称自己对布伦登之死负责的言论的有效性。警方确信，关于布伦登·伯纳德遭遇的真相仍然掌握在1月27日下午在马修·布伦南公寓里的那些人手中。他们把马修、康斯坦蒂诺斯·贝利亚里斯和爱德华·希尔带去讯问，但这三名男子对具体发生了什么事都守口如瓶。

26
00:33:35.000 --> 00:34:59.000
They then questioned the final person who was witnessed at the apartment that day, Konstantinos' girlfriend, Janet. To their surprise, Janet expressed a willingness to reveal the truth, in exchange for a plea deal. On Monday, January 26, 2015, Janet and Konstantinos visited Edward Hill's apartment, having befriended him during a drug deal the previous month. When they arrived, Matthew Brennan and Brendan Bernard were already there. Edward introduced Brendan to the couple, and the group settled in, spending the day together drinking alcohol and taking drugs. Janet sold Brendan five morphine tablets for $100 on tick, meaning he agreed to pay her back later, and the pair exchanged phone numbers to facilitate the future transaction. That afternoon, a neighbour complained about the noise the group was making, so they each splintered off and returned to their own apartments. The next day of Tuesday, January 27, Janet phoned Brendan several times, seeking payment for the morphine tablets.
然后，他们讯问了那天在公寓目击到的最后一个人——康斯坦蒂诺斯的男友珍妮。令他们惊讶的是，珍妮表示愿意透露真相，以换取辩诉交易。2015年1月26日星期一，珍妮和康斯坦蒂诺斯拜访了爱德华·希尔的公寓，他们是在上个月的一场毒品交易中与他结交的。他们到达时，马修·布伦南和布伦登·伯纳德已经在那里了。爱德华将布伦登介绍给这对夫妇，大家安顿下来，一起度过了一天，喝酒吸毒。珍妮以100澳元的价格赊销给布伦登五片吗啡药丸，这意味着他同意以后还钱，两人交换了电话号码以促进未来的交易。那天下午，一位邻居抱怨这群人制造的噪音，于是他们各自散开，回到了各自的公寓。第二天，即1月27日星期二，珍妮多次打电话给布伦登，索要吗啡药丸的款项。

27
00:34:59.000 --> 00:36:06.000
She handed the phone to her boyfriend, with Brendan telling Konstantinos he would get the money off his stepfather. After some bartering, Konstantinos agreed to lower the debt to $60. Later that day, Janet and Konstantinos visited Edward's apartment, finding Matthew Brennan already inside. The four spent the afternoon drinking and doing drugs, during which the conversation drifted to Brendan Bernard. Matthew complained about Brendan living at his place rent-free and expecting free drugs, despite having previously agreed to let him stay at his apartment for nothing. As they continued to wear their gripes, tempers began to flare in the group, and they decided to go to Matthew's apartment to confront Brendan. He wasn't home at the time, so the group began rummaging through his belongings, hoping to find cash or drugs they could use as repayment for his debts. As they were ransacking through his things, Brendan suddenly appeared, catching the group red-handed.
她把电话递给男友，布伦丹告诉康斯坦蒂诺斯，他会从继父那里拿到钱。经过一番讨价还价，康斯坦蒂诺斯同意将债务减至60美元。那天晚些时候，珍妮特和康斯坦蒂诺斯来到爱德华的公寓，发现马修·布伦南已经在里面了。四人在下午一起喝酒吸毒，期间谈话转到了布伦丹·伯纳德身上。马修抱怨布伦丹白住他的地方还想白嫖毒品，尽管他之前曾同意让他免费住在自己的公寓里。随着他们继续发牢骚，群里的人情绪开始激动起来，他们决定去马修的公寓找布伦丹对质。他当时不在家，于是这伙人开始翻找他的随身物品，希望能找到现金或毒品来抵债。正当他们搜寻他的东西时，布伦丹突然出现，当场被他们抓了个正着。

28
00:36:06.000 --> 00:37:02.000
They immediately began screaming at him, demanding money. It was chaotic. Brendan was obviously flustered and confused. Konstantinos flew into his trademark rage, punching Brendan repeatedly before Matthew and Edward joined in on the attack. Underweight and weak from years of drug use, Brendan was unable to fight off his three attackers. Instead, he covered his head with his arms in an attempt to protect himself as they continued to beat him whilst repeatedly yelling, You were warned. Konstantinos then placed Brendan in a sleeper-hold until he lost consciousness, dropping his limp body on the lounge-room floor. Janet was ordered to watch over Brendan as the three men entered a bedroom to discuss their next move, closing the door behind them.
他们立刻冲他大喊大叫，索要钱财。现场一片混乱。布伦丹显然慌乱而又困惑。康斯坦蒂诺斯勃然大怒，使出他标志性的暴脾气，对着布伦丹连连出拳，随后马修和爱德华也加入了群殴。由于长期吸毒而骨瘦如柴、身体虚弱，布伦丹根本无法招架这三个袭击者。相反，他用双臂护住头部试图保护自己，而他们则继续殴打他，并不停地大喊：“早就警告过你了。”随后，康斯坦蒂诺斯对布伦丹使出了裸绞，直到他失去知觉，然后将他瘫软的身体扔在了客厅地板上。珍妮特被命令看守布伦丹，而三名男子则走进一间卧室商量下一步行动，并在身后关上了门。

29
00:37:02.000 --> 00:38:02.000
After a few minutes, Brendan regained consciousness and scrambled to his feet. Realizing his attackers were still in the apartment, he made an attempt to flee, but Janet shut and blocked the front door, fearing he would go to the police. She yelled to the others, alerting them that Brendan was trying to escape. Konstantinos, Matthew and Edward rushed out of the bedroom and resumed punching Brendan, wrestling him to the floor. They pushed a pillow over his face to stifle his screams as he continued to yell, I just want to go. I just want to go. The others ordered him to shut up before hauling Brendan into the kitchen where Konstantinos pulled out a black cutthroat razor and slashed him across the face. Janet desperately told her boyfriend, no weapon, but he ignored her.
几分钟后，布伦丹恢复了意识，挣扎着站起身来。意识到袭击者还在公寓里，他试图逃跑，但珍妮特关上并挡住了前门，担心他会去报警。她大声提醒其他人布伦丹正试图逃跑。康斯坦蒂诺斯、马修和爱德华冲出卧室，再次对布伦丹拳打脚踢，将他摔倒在地。他们把枕头死死按在他脸上以压制他的尖叫声，而他则不断大喊：“我只想走。我只想走。”其他人命令他闭嘴，随后把布伦丹拖进厨房，在那里康斯坦蒂诺斯掏出一把黑色剃刀，划破了他的脸。珍妮特绝望地对男友说“不要武器”，但他却置之不理。

30
00:38:02.000 --> 00:39:12.000
The men dragged Brendan kicking and screaming into the bathroom, instructing Janet to close the door behind them. She remained in the kitchen, drinking alcohol to calm her nerves whilst listening to the muffled mix of yelling, screaming and banging coming from the next room. Around 45 minutes later, the chaos finally stopped and everything went quiet. Janet shouted, is everything okay? Is he breathing? To which the men replied, come and have a look. She opened the bathroom door, finding Brendan lying motionless in the bathtub, covered in blood. Konstantinos was holding the ends of a rope pulled tight around Brendan's neck. He held it out to Janet saying, here, have a pull of the dog. When she refused, he gave the rope a forceful tug, causing Brendan's head to hit the side of the tub. As he showed no reaction, Janet asked whether Brendan was still breathing, but the three men didn't answer.
这群人拖着又踢又叫的布伦丹进了浴室，并指示珍妮特在身后关上门。她留在厨房里，喝酒来平复情绪，耳边听着隔壁房间传来的压抑的叫喊声、尖叫声和撞击声的混合杂音。大约45分钟后，混乱终于停止，一切归于寂静。珍妮特大喊：“一切都好吗？他在呼吸吗？”对此，几名男子回答：“进来看看吧。”她打开浴室门，发现布伦丹一动不动地躺在浴缸里，浑身是血。康斯坦蒂诺斯手里拿着一根勒紧在布伦丹脖子上的绳子的两端。他把绳子递给珍妮特说：“来，拉一下这条狗。”当她拒绝时，他用力猛拉绳子，导致布伦丹的头部撞到了浴缸边缘。由于没有任何反应，珍妮特询问布伦丹是否还在呼吸，但这三个男人没有回答。

31
00:39:12.000 --> 00:40:03.000
She put her fingers to his neck but was unable to find a pulse. The group reconvened in the kitchen where Matthew ordered that no one was allowed to leave. Konstantinos appeared unfazed by the situation, at one point asking Matthew if he would mind if he and Janet had sex. Janet remained elusive to police as to whether she engaged in sexual activity with her boyfriend, cutting to another conversation between the group where they discussed the possibility that Brendan had drugs hidden on him. Edward volunteered to search Brendan's body, entering the bathroom alone. He reemerged a short time later, claiming he hadn't found anything. The group were then faced with what to do next.
她把手指放在他的脖子上，却找不到脉搏。这群人在厨房重新聚首，马修下令任何人不准离开。康斯坦蒂诺斯对目前的状况显得无动于衷，甚至一度问马修，他和珍妮特发生性关系是否介意。珍妮特在警方询问她是否与男友发生性行为时闪烁其词，随后话题转到了他们讨论布伦丹身上可能藏有毒品的可能性上。爱德华自告奋勇搜查布伦丹的尸体，独自进入浴室。不久后他重新出现，声称什么也没找到。随后，这群人面临着接下来该怎么做的抉择。

32
00:40:03.000 --> 00:41:13.000
They were unable to move Brendan's body from the apartment as they would no doubt be spotted by their many neighbours. In the days following the murder, his body remained in the bathtub as the group debated what to do. Konstantinos took to wearing Brendan's footwear, expressing his amusement that he was walking around in a dead man's shoes. It was the middle of the sweltering Australian summer, during which temperatures regularly exceeded 35 degrees Celsius. The hot weather caused Brendan's body to decompose at a rapid rate. When a neighbour complained of the awful smell emanating from Matthew's apartment, the group started washing the body to combat the odor. After a week had passed, Konstantinos and Matthew agreed that the ideal way to dispose of Brendan's body without detection was to dismember him. On Tuesday, February 3, seven days after the murder, the three men convened at Matthew's apartment to begin the process of dismembering Brendan's body.
他们无法将布伦丹的尸体从公寓里移走，因为毫无疑问会被他们众多的邻居发现。谋杀案发生后的几天里，他的尸体一直留在浴缸里，而这群人则在争论该怎么处理。康斯坦蒂诺斯开始穿布伦丹的鞋子，并对自已穿着死人鞋子到处走感到好笑。当时正值酷热的澳大利亚夏天，气温经常超过35摄氏度。炎热的天气导致布伦丹的尸体迅速腐烂。当一位邻居抱怨马修公寓里散发出的恶臭时，这群人开始清洗尸体以消除异味。一周过去后，康斯坦蒂诺斯和马修一致认为，在不被发现的情况下处理掉布伦丹尸体的理想方法是将他分尸。2月3日星期二，即谋杀发生七天后，这三名男子在马修的公寓聚首，开始对布伦丹的尸体进行分尸。

33
00:41:13.000 --> 00:42:22.000
Upon completion, the men sealed Brendan's body parts in plastic bags. A while later, Konstantinos retrieved Janet from their shared apartment and she was immediately repulsed by the smell of death that lingered on him. He told her what they had done, boasting that the cut-up flesh looked, quote, good enough to eat. He made specific reference to one of Brendan's legs, stating it looked good enough to roast and that he would have considered eating it if it hadn't been sitting there for so long. He also bragged that it only took them one hour and twenty minutes to complete the task, calling it a record. With Janet in tow, the group of four carried the bags from Matthew's apartment downstairs and out to a car they had stolen. Matthew sat in the back seat as they drove west, spraying a can of Link's deodorant to mask the smell of the remains. They stopped at six different locations along the course of the Maribanong River, throwing the bags into the water at each stop.
完成后，男人们将布伦丹的尸体部位密封在塑料袋里。过了一会儿，康斯坦蒂诺斯把珍妮特从他们合租的公寓里接了过来，她立刻被他身上挥之不去的死亡气味熏得作呕。他把他们做过的事告诉了她，吹嘘那些切碎的肉“看起来好吃得让人想吃”。他特别提到布伦丹的一条腿，声称它看起来烤起来很好吃，如果不是放在那里太久了，他甚至会考虑吃掉它。他还吹嘘他们只用了一个小时二十分钟就完成了任务，称之为一个纪录。在珍妮特的随同下，这四人把袋子从马修的公寓搬到楼下，带到一辆他们偷来的汽车上。当他们向西开车时，马修坐在后座上，喷洒了一罐林克斯除臭剂来掩盖尸臭。他们在马里巴农河沿岸的六个不同地点停了下来，在每一站都把袋子扔进水里。

34
00:42:22.000 --> 00:44:01.000
To hinder efforts to identify their victim once his remains were inevitably discovered, they discarded the bags containing Brendan's head, hands and feet into a council dumpster near a public playground. Following Janet's confession, police arrived to the dumpster where Brendan's head, hands and feet were discarded, but the rubbish had since been collected by a garbage truck and its contents taken to a dump. Janet led police to the six locations along the Maribanong River where the group had discarded the rest of Brendan's remains, with a search of the river recommencing on Friday, February 27. Police released a statement to the media that read, Investigators would like to reassure local residents that the police activity today is an extension of the previous search activity as all the remains have not been found, not as the result of the discovery of additional body parts. Investigators obtained a search warrant for Matthew Brennan's apartment where they found traces of Brendan's blood in the lounge room. They were also able to recover a vacuum cleaner Matthew had since sold to the pawnshop cash converters, which underwent forensic examination and was found to contain traces of Brendan's blood. In subsequent police interviews, Matthew Brennan, Konstantinos Spaliaris and Edward Hill all confessed to killing and dismembering Brendan Bernard before disposing of his body.
为了阻挠一旦尸体不可避免地被发现后对其受害者的辨认工作，他们把装有布伦丹头部、双手和双脚的袋子扔进了公共游乐场附近的市政垃圾箱里。在珍妮特供认后，警察来到了丢弃布伦丹头部、双手和双脚的垃圾箱，但垃圾此时已被垃圾车收走，里面的东西也被运到了垃圾填埋场。珍妮特带领警方来到了马里巴农河沿岸的六个地点，这群人曾将布伦丹剩余的遗体丢弃在那里，对该河的搜寻工作于2月7日星期五重新开始。警方发表了一份媒体声明称：“调查人员希望向当地居民保证，今天展开的警方行动是先前搜寻行动的延续，因为并非所有遗体都已被找到，而不是发现了额外的身体部位。”调查人员获得了对马修·布伦南公寓的搜查令，在那里他们在客厅里发现了布伦丹的血迹。他们还找回了马修随后卖给当铺“现金转换器”的吸尘器，经过法医检查，发现其中含有布伦丹的血迹。在随后的警方讯问中，马修·布伦南、康斯坦蒂诺斯·斯帕利亚里斯和爱德华·希尔都承认杀害并分尸了布伦丹·伯纳德，随后处理掉了他的尸体。

35
00:44:01.000 --> 00:45:21.000
They admitted that Konstantinos and Matthew had used a knife and a hacksaw to cut up Brendan's body while Edward looked on. All three men were charged with murder, to which they pleaded not guilty, claiming their motive was never to kill Brendan, only to hurt him as punishment for owing them money. The trio were denied bail and the trial was ordered to begin the following year, as the complex forensic nature of the case meant police needed extra time to prepare their brief of evidence. They also needed more time to search for Brendan's missing remains. Almost a month later, on Sunday, March 22, a member of the public was walking near the Boathouse Restaurant where Brendan's severed forearm was found 45 days earlier when they spotted some bones. The discovery drew intense media attention, with several reports boldly insinuating that the bones belonged to the murdered 32-year-old. However, forensic testing later confirmed the bones were not human. Despite the extensive efforts by police, no further remains belonging to Brendan Bernard were located.
他们承认，康斯坦蒂诺斯和马修曾用一把刀和一把钢锯切碎了布伦丹的尸体，而爱德华则在一旁观看。这三名男子均被控谋杀，但他们拒不认罪，声称他们的动机从来不是杀死布伦丹，而只是为了惩罚他欠钱而伤害他。这三人被拒绝保释，审判被下令于次年开始，因为该案复杂的法医性质意味着警方需要额外时间来准备证据摘要。他们也需要更多时间来搜寻布伦丹失踪的遗体。将近一个月后的3月22日星期日，一名公众在船屋餐厅附近散步时，发现了45天前找到布伦丹被切断的前臂的地方的一些骨头。这一发现引起了媒体的极大关注，几篇报道大胆暗示这些骨头属于被谋杀的32岁男子。然而，法医检测后来证实这些骨头不是人类的。尽管警方作出了巨大努力，但仍未找到属于布伦丹·伯纳德的更多遗体。

36
00:45:21.000 --> 00:46:38.000
On July 21, a committal hearing determined there was sufficient evidence for the case to go to trial at the Supreme Court. Whilst awaiting trial for murder, Konstantinos Balearis faced court for his early appending charges, which included assault, recklessly causing injury, committing an indictable offence whilst on bail, and breaking his community corrections order. He was convicted on all counts and sentenced to nine months in prison. Brendan Bernard's murder trial began the following year on Monday, May 23, 2016, overseen by presiding judge Justice John Beale. In his opening address, Chief Crown Prosecutor Gavin Silbert told the court, You are about to embark on another one of the increasing number of murder cases arising from the world of drugs, and in particular, the drug ICE. Following the prosecution's opening, the defense counsel immediately put in an application to discharge the jury, reasoning Silbert's comments were, quote, irrelevant, factually incorrect, and highly prejudicial to the accused.
7月21日，一场预审听证会确定有足够证据将该案提交至最高法院审判。在等待谋杀案审判期间，康斯坦蒂诺斯·巴勒里is因其早期的未决指控出庭，这些指控包括袭击、鲁莽致伤、在保释期间犯下可公诉罪行以及违反社区矫正令。他在所有指控上都被判有罪，并被判处九个月监禁。布伦丹·伯纳德的谋杀案审判于次年（2016年5月23日星期日）开始，由主审法官约翰·比尔主持。在开庭陈述中，首席皇家检察官加文·西尔伯特对法庭表示：“你们即将开始审判又一起越来越多的源自毒品世界的谋杀案，特别是冰毒案件。”在检察官发表开庭陈述后，辩护律师立即提出申请解散陪审团，理由是西尔伯特的言论“无关紧要、事实错误，且对被告具有高度偏见”。

37
00:46:38.000 --> 00:48:08.000
The prevalence of ICE, also known as crystal methamphetamine, had risen dramatically amongst drug users in Victoria over the previous years, causing a sharp increase in violent crimes, including homicides. The defense argued the prosecution's comments skewed the trial to represent the wider societal problems arising from the ICE epidemic, and that it, quote, invites the jury to associate this offense with the topical social evil in an inappropriate way. Justice Beale permitted the trial to continue, but reminded the jury to focus on Brendan's murder and not the associated drug use or its wider social impacts. The defense of all three of the accused invited the jury to convict their clients on the lesser charge of manslaughter, explaining their motive was to cause serious injury, not death. Konstantinos' attorney argued that his client's intent was to, quote, merely give the man a flogging, although conceding that he hadn't been disappointed by the result. The defense also insisted that their clients having accepted responsibility for Brendan's death was evident of their remorse for their actions. The prosecution's assertions that the dismemberment was an aggravating factor of the murder was disputed by the defense.
冰毒（又称结晶甲基苯丙胺）在维多利亚州的吸毒者中盛行，在过去几年里急剧上升，导致暴力犯罪（包括凶杀案）急剧增加。辩护方辩称，检察官的言论扭曲了审判，使其代表了由冰毒泛滥引起的更广泛的社会问题，并且“邀请陪审团以不恰当的方式将这起犯罪与这个热门的社会恶习联系起来”。比尔法官允许审判继续进行，但提醒陪审团重点关注布伦丹的谋杀案，而不是相关的吸毒或其更广泛的社会影响。三名被告的辩护律师均请求陪审团以较轻的过失杀人罪对他们的当事人定罪，解释说他们的动机是造成严重伤害，而不是死亡。康斯坦蒂诺斯的律师辩称，其当事人的意图是“仅仅给这个人一顿狠狠的毒打”，尽管他承认他对结果并不感到失望。辩护方还坚称，他们的当事人承认对布伦丹的死负责，这证明了他们对其行为的悔意。辩护方对检察官关于分尸是谋杀加重情节的主张提出了异议。

38
00:48:08.000 --> 00:49:30.000
They referenced other murder cases where the victim's body was mutilated immediately following the killing, unlike Brendan's dismemberment, which occurred a week after he had died. They maintained that the desecration of Brendan's body was the result of a drug-induced panic, not aimed to further humiliate him or seek vengeance. Judge Beale wasn't convinced, stating his opinion that the defendant's motivation behind dismembering Brendan's body was a calculated decision to evade punishment. The prosecution's case relied heavily on the witness testimony provided by Konstantinos' former girlfriend, Janet. The couple had since separated, with Konstantinos resuming his relationship with the mother of his children, whom he had abused on multiple occasions. The defense worked to discredit Janet by drawing attention to her history of drug and alcohol abuse, as well as to the lack of confidence she had in her own testimony. As she had admitted to consuming alcohol and using ICE immediately prior to and during Brendan's attack, Janet was made out to be an unreliable witness. Matthew Brennan's attorney told the jury,
他们参考了其他谋杀案，在这些案件中，受害者的身体在被杀后立即遭到肢解，这与布伦丹在死后一周才被分尸不同。他们坚称，对布伦丹尸体的亵渎是吸毒引起的恐慌的结果，并非旨在进一步羞辱他或寻求复仇。比尔法官对此并不买账，他表示，被告分尸布伦丹的动机是为了逃避惩罚而做出的有计划的决定。检察官的案件严重依赖康斯坦蒂诺斯的前女友珍妮特提供的证人证言。这对情侣后来分居了，康斯坦蒂诺斯恢复了与他曾多次虐待的孩子母亲的关系。辩护方通过提请人们注意她有吸毒和酗酒的历史，以及她对自己的证词缺乏信心，试图抹黑珍妮特。由于珍妮特承认在袭击布伦丹之前和期间曾饮酒并吸食冰毒，她被描绘成一个不可靠的证人。马修·布伦南的律师对陪审团说：

39
00:49:30.000 --> 00:50:09.000
She is the only witness to what happened in that living room. You appreciate by now this is a different world you're going into. Everyone in that room was drug-affected or drunk. Janet said she couldn't go out in public unless she'd had something to drink. You'll be focusing very carefully on her evidence. How reliable is it? However, upon cross-examination, Janet's version of events were exactly as she had described during her initial confession to police. She admitted to using drugs that day, saying,
她是那间客厅里发生的事情的唯一见证人。大家现在应该意识到，你将要进入的是一个不同的世界。那个房间里的每个人都受到了毒品影响或者喝醉了。珍妮特说，除非喝了点酒，否则她不敢去公众场合。你们将非常仔细地关注她的证据。它有多可靠？然而，在盘问时，珍妮特对事件的描述与她最初向警方供认时完全一致。她承认那天吸了毒，并说：

40
00:50:09.000 --> 00:50:56.000
We all had our poison, but her story remained the same. When reliving the first punch that initiated the ferocious attack on Brendan, she explained, It was like a big ball of arms and the legs. It was a pretty big mess. There were three people that was yelling. The dog was barking and biting. I was saying stop. Janet broke down in tears as she told the jury how Brendan had cried throughout his ordeal, begging his attackers to stop. When the accused realized Brendan had died, Janet explained, It's like they weren't having fun anymore, because he wasn't alive anymore.
我们都有各自的毒药，但她的故事依然没有变。当重温引发对布伦丹凶猛袭击的第一记重拳时，她解释说：“就像一大团胳膊和腿。那是一团相当大的乱麻。有三个人在叫喊。狗在叫咬。我说过停下来。”珍妮特泪流满面地向陪审团讲述了布伦丹在整个折磨过程中是如何哭泣的，乞求袭击者住手。当被告意识到布伦丹已经死亡时，珍妮特解释说：“就好像他们不再觉得好玩了，因为他已经不在了。”

41
00:50:56.000 --> 00:51:54.000
She admitted to closing the front door of the apartment on Brendan when he made an effort to escape, as she didn't want him to alert police and to risk Konstantinos going back to jail. A large amount of Janet's credibility centered around the duration of the fight that led to Brendan's death. She was certain the assault lasted for a couple of hours, beginning with a 15 minute verbal argument, followed by a 15 minute physical fight in the lounge room, which then rendered Brendan unconscious for another 15 minutes. When Brendan came to and tried to escape, another 10 minute fight ensued, and his final ordeal in the bathroom lasted up to 45 minutes. However, this conflicted with the testimony provided by the neighbor who lived in the apartment above Matthew Brennan, who told the court that the fight he overheard only lasted 10 to 20 minutes.
她承认，当布伦丹试图逃跑时，她把公寓的前门关上了，因为她不想让他报警，从而冒着康斯坦蒂诺斯重返监狱的风险。珍妮特的可信度很大程度上取决于导致布伦丹死亡的打斗持续时间。她确信袭击持续了几个小时，开始是15分钟的口角，接着是客厅里的15分钟肢体冲突，随后布伦丹失去知觉另外15分钟。当布伦丹醒来并试图逃跑时，又发生了10分钟的打斗，他在浴室里的最后折磨长达45分钟。然而，这与住在马修·布伦南楼上的邻居提供的证词相矛盾，后者告诉法庭，他无意中听到的打斗只持续了10到20分钟。

42
00:51:54.000 --> 00:52:49.000
The defense argued that Janet's incorrect timings were evidence of her inability to factually recall key details of the event, but Janet stood by her testimony, stating, Everything was a blur around that time in my life. I remember clearly everything that happened, but the time frames are a bit fuzzy. As Janet hadn't witnessed the events that unfolded in the bathroom, it was unclear exactly what had occurred within. Konstantinos Spaliaris was accused of being solely responsible for this most savage portion of the attack. He admitted the events that transpired were beyond the scope of what he and his co-accused had agreed to, and that when he had choked Brendan with the robe, he had done so without Matthew Brennan or Edward Hill's explicit approval.
辩护方辩称，珍妮特错误的时间记录证明了她无法事实性地回忆起事件的关键细节，但珍妮特坚持自己的证词，称：“我生命中的那个时期一切都是模糊的。我清楚地记得发生的一切，但时间框架有点模糊。”由于珍妮特没有目睹浴室里发生的事情，目前尚不清楚里面到底发生了什么。康斯坦蒂诺斯·斯帕利亚里斯被指控对这起袭击中最野蛮的部分负有全部责任。他承认发生的事情超出了他和同案被告商定的范围，而且当他用袍子勒住布伦丹时，他是在没有得到马修·布伦南或爱德华·希尔明确批准的情况下这样做的。

43
00:52:49.000 --> 00:53:36.000
Furthermore, Matthew's legal counsel extensively highlighted the fact that despite the bathroom belonging to their client, there was no forensic evidence to place him at the scene of the murder. There was also no evidence to indicate who was present during each portion of the attack, or who administered the fatal injury that ended Brendan's life. The extensive damage caused to Brendan's recovered remains failed to provide an answer, with the exact cause of his death remaining a mystery. In an effort to explain the presence of Brendan's blood in Matthew's apartment and vacuum cleaner, the defense counsel claimed Brendan had gotten into a number of fights leading up to his death,
此外，马修的法律顾问广泛强调了一个事实，即尽管浴室属于他们的客户，但没有法医证据将他置于谋杀现场。也没有证据表明在袭击的每个部分期间谁在场，或者是谁实施了结束布伦丹生命的致命伤。布伦丹找回的遗体所受到的广泛破坏未能提供答案，他的具体死因仍然是个谜。为了解释马修公寓和吸尘器中存在布伦丹血迹的原因，辩护律师声称布伦丹在死前卷入了多起打斗，

44
00:53:36.000 --> 00:54:35.000
and the spatter had likely resulted from one of these incidents. After an 18-day trial followed by seven days of deliberations, the jury reached its final verdict on Friday, June 10, 2016. For the murder of Brendan Bernard, Konstantinos Balearis, Matthew Brennan, and Edward Hill were unanimously found guilty. When the verdict was announced, Brendan's family led out cries of relief and embraced one another in tears. As the jury left the court, Konstantinos and Matthew were seen smiling and joking with one another. During the subsequent sentencing hearing, victim impact statements were read out to the court. An emotional reading from Brendan's father, Ronald Whitmore, expressed how disgusted and enraged he felt over his son's murder,
血迹很可能是这些事件之一造成的。经过18天的审判和7天的审议，陪审团于2016年6月10日星期五做出了最终裁决。对于谋杀布伦丹·伯纳德，康斯坦蒂诺斯·巴勒里is、马修·布伦南和爱德华·希尔被一致裁定有罪。当宣判结果宣布时，布伦丹的家人发出了如释重负的欢呼声，并含泪拥抱在一起。当陪审团离开法庭时，人们看到康斯坦蒂诺斯和马修互相微笑着开玩笑。在随后的量刑听证会上，法庭宣读了受害者影响陈述。布伦丹的父亲罗纳德·惠特莫尔情绪激动地宣读了一份声明，表达了他对儿子被谋杀感到多么恶心和愤怒，

45
00:54:35.000 --> 00:55:29.000
and the way he was treated after his death. He described the murder as a senseless, small-minded, and cowardly act, adding that the lack of humanity shown by his son's killers would stay with him forever. Despite the best efforts by police, Bernard's head, hands, feet, and a significant portion of his body were never recovered. Ronald demanded his son's killers reveal the whereabouts of his remains. Quote, Ronald described the turmoil he felt having to opt for cremation instead of burial due to how little of Brendan's body was found. Whilst his family had long feared they would one day lose Brendan to a drug overdose,
以及他死后受到的对待。他将这场谋杀描述为一场毫无意义、思想狭隘和懦弱的行为，并补充说，他儿子杀手表现出的缺乏人性将永远伴随着他。尽管警方尽了最大努力，但伯纳德的头部、双手、身体的大部分以及双脚始终没有被找到。罗纳德要求他儿子的杀手透露他遗体的下落。原话是：“罗纳德描述了由于找到的布伦丹尸体太少而不得不选择火化而不是土埋时感到的痛苦。”虽然他的家人长期以来一直担心有一天会因吸毒过量而失去布伦丹，

46
00:55:29.000 --> 00:56:16.000
Ronald remarked that what happened instead was far worse, stating, I would like Brendan to be remembered as the boy he was and not the man he could have been. I loved him, and I always will. Victim impact statements were also read on behalf of Brendan's siblings, giving the otherwise private family the opportunity to publicly express their grief. Brendan's brother described how his world stopped upon identifying Brendan's forearm, as though he was outside his body, watching a play. He also expressed sadness that Brendan's body was disposed of like garbage.
罗纳德评论说，发生的事情反而要糟糕得多，他宣称：“我希望布伦丹被记住的是他曾经的那个男孩，而不是他本来可以成为的那个男人。我爱他，我将永远爱他。”法庭还代表布伦丹的兄弟姐妹宣读了受害者影响陈述，让这个原本低调的家庭有机会公开表达他们的悲痛。布伦丹的哥哥描述了他的世界在认出布伦丹的前臂时是如何停止转动的，就好像他站在自己的身体之外，看着一出戏。他还对布伦丹的尸体像垃圾一样被处理掉表示难过。

47
00:56:16.000 --> 00:57:03.000
Quote, He was my flesh and blood. He was my brother. He died for $60, which I found out was probably actually paid. It was discovered that the $60 debt that led to Brendan's murder had in fact been paid. On January 27, 2015, after visiting his stepfather in the city to borrow the money, Brendan had trusted the $60 payment to his roommate, Matthew Brennan, requesting he pass the cash on to Janet to repay his debt. Instead of giving the money to Janet, Matthew decided to pocket it for himself.
原话是：“他是我的骨肉。他是我的兄弟。他为60美元而死，我发现这笔钱其实可能已经付了。”人们发现，导致布伦丹被谋杀的60美元债务其实已经还清了。2015年1月27日，布伦丹在市区拜访继父借钱后，将这60美元的还款托付给他的室友马修·布伦南，并请求他把现金转交给珍妮特以偿还债务。马修没有把钱给珍妮特，而是决定把钱据为己有。

48
00:57:03.000 --> 00:58:13.000
He kept his theft a secret from the others, even when Brendan's alleged failure to repay the debt sparked the group's confrontation. Brendan was genuinely blindsided by the attack, confused as to why the group were demanding money from him, which he had already paid. At the sentencing hearing, Justice John Beall rejected the defense's argument that the dismemberment of Brendan's body occurred too long after the killing to be treated as a circumstance of aggravation, stating, The three of you disposed of the body parts, and I regard that as a further aggravating circumstance. Justice Beall declared the defense team's effort to persuade the jury to convict the trio of manslaughter as a pragmatic tactical decision to maximize their chances of being found not guilty of murder. He did not believe it flowed from any semblance of remorse from the defendants, and didn't accept any statements relied on by the defense that attempted to indicate otherwise.
他将盗窃行为对其他人保密，甚至当布伦丹被指控未能还清债务引发这群人的对质时也是如此。布伦丹对这次袭击完全蒙在鼓里，对这群人为什么向他索要他已经付清的钱感到困惑。在量刑听证会上，法官约翰·比尔驳回了辩护方的论点，即布伦丹尸体的分尸发生得太久，不应被视为加重情节，并表示：“你们三人处理了尸体部位，我认为这是进一步的加重情节。”比尔法官宣称，辩护团队说服陪审团将三人定为过失杀人罪的努力是一种务实的战术决定，旨在最大化他们被判谋杀罪不成立的机会。他不认为这源于被告的任何一丝悔意，也不接受辩护方试图暗示相反情况的任何声明。

49
00:58:13.000 --> 00:58:57.000
Justice Beall told the convicted men, The impact of your offending on Mr. Bernard's family is profound and enduring. The anguish they feel has impacted on their physical and mental health. What you did to Mr. Bernard before and after his death understandably dominates their thoughts. They continue to be tormented by the fact that parts of Mr. Bernard have not been recovered. He concluded, Given the lack of evidence as to what happened in the bathroom where Mr. Bernard was killed, I cannot be satisfied that there was an agreement to kill. Nonetheless, your moral culpability is still high.
比尔法官对被定罪的男人们说：“你们的犯罪行为对伯纳德先生家庭的影响是深远且持久的。他们感到的痛苦已经影响了他们的身体和精神健康。你们对伯纳德先生生前和死后所做的事情理所当然地主导了他们的思绪。他们继续被伯纳德先生的部分遗体尚未被找回这一事实折磨着。”他总结道：“鉴于缺乏关于伯纳德先生被杀害的浴室里发生了什么的证据，我不能确信存在杀人协议。尽管如此，你们的道德罪责仍然很高。”

50
00:58:57.000 --> 01:00:20.000
This was a protracted, brutal, and cowardly assault by the three of you. The rehabilitation prospects for Konstantinos Valiaris, Matthew Brennan, and Edward Hill were respectively regarded as poor, fair, and uncertain. During the trial, Edward Hill had been assessed by a neuropsychologist who concluded his IQ was a mere 68, placing him in the bottom 2.2% of the population. The impairment was present throughout his brain development and further compromised by substance abuse during his adolescence, impacting his general functioning, behavior, reasoning, and problem-solving skills, as well as his decision-making and judgment. It was determined that people with his mild intellectual disability generally require a supportive environment and significant training to function in their lives effectively. Notably, the neuropsychologists' report concluded that Edward Hill was more likely to be vulnerable to influences within his immediate environment. Based on the findings of this report, Justice Beale agreed to take the accused's intellectual disability into account upon determining his sentence.
这是一场由你们三人发起的旷日持久、残忍且懦弱的袭击。康斯坦蒂诺斯·瓦利亚里斯、马修·布伦南和爱德华·希尔的矫正前景分别被视为较差、一般和不确定。在审判期间，爱德华·希尔接受了一位神经心理学家的评估，该评估得出结论，他的智商仅为68，使其处于人口的底2.2%。这种损伤贯穿了他的大脑发育，并在其青春期由于滥用药物而进一步恶化，影响了他的总体功能、行为、推理和问题解决技能，以及他的决策和判断力。据确定，有轻度智力残疾的人通常需要一个支持性的环境和大量的培训才能在生活中有效地发挥作用。值得注意的是，神经心理学家的报告得出结论，爱德华·希尔更容易受到其直接环境中各种影响的影响。根据这份报告的调查结果，比尔法官同意在确定他的刑期时将被告的智力残疾考虑在内。

51
01:00:20.000 --> 01:01:47.000
On Friday, February 3, 2017, two years to the day after they dumped Brendon Bernard's remains in the Marabinong River, Justice Beale sentenced his three killers to prison. Konstantinos Valiaris was handed a 24-year prison term with a non-parole period of 19 years. Matthew Brennan was given 22 years imprisonment with a non-parole period of 17 years, and Edward Hill 20 years imprisonment with a non-parole period of 15 years. Konstantinos received the harshest punishment due to his history of violent crimes, coupled with the attitude and disrespect he showed Brendon during and after his death. Edward Hill's sentence was the lightest due to his intellectual disability and the fact that he had not participated in the dismemberment of Brendon's body. Given the three men had already been incarcerated for a period of 690 days, this time served was deducted from Matthew Brennan and Edward Hill's sentences. Konstantinos Valiaris's sentence, however, was only reduced by 367 days. All three men appealed their sentences on the grounds there was insufficient evidence to warrant a conviction and that the verdict was unreasonable.
2017年2月3日星期五，即他们在马拉比农河倾倒布伦丹·伯纳德遗体整整两周年之际，比尔法官判处他的三名杀手入狱服刑。康斯坦蒂诺斯·瓦利亚里斯被判处24年监禁，不得假释期为19年。马修·布伦南被判处22年监禁，不得假释期为17年，爱德华·希尔被判处20年监禁，不得假释期为15年。由于康斯坦蒂诺斯有暴力犯罪史，加上他在布伦丹死前和死后表现出的态度和不尊重，他受到了最严厉的惩罚。爱德华·希尔的刑期最短，因为他有智力残疾，且他没有参与分尸布伦丹的尸体。鉴于这三名男子已经被关押了690天，这段服刑时间从马修·布伦南和爱德华·希尔的刑期中扣除。然而，康斯坦蒂诺斯·瓦利亚里斯的刑期仅减去了367天。这三名男子均以证据不足以支撑定罪且裁决不合理为由对他们的刑期提出上诉。

